; Provider-route executable family, 1 of 7 — the happy path, and the
; only case in the family whose point is that *nothing* is diagnosed.
;
; `(shader …)` carries an opaque string. On the identity route a
; cross-ref would read one symbol off each instance's `:name`; here the
; validator instead hands `:src` to the `lines` provider, and every name
; that comes back is registered as a member of `lines/shader`. So the two
; references below resolve against names that exist nowhere in the
; document's own syntax — they are inside the blob, and only the provider
; can see them.
;
; `:name main` is still just a key on the form: the provider route does
; not read it, and it is here to show that it does not.
(use-plugin "lines")

(shader :name main :src "u_time\nu_res")

(bind :uniform u_time)
(bind :uniform u_res)
